<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="open-pilgrimages" version="1.1"><metadata><name>Camino Portugués (Central)</name><desc>The second most-walked route to Santiago de Compostela, traversing the Minho region of northern Portugal before crossing the Miño river border at Tui and continuing through Galicia. Walked since the 12th century. Shorter, flatter, and less crowded than the Camino Francés, with a distinctive sequence of Romanesque churches, medieval stone villages, and the iconic river-crossing from Portugal into Spain.</desc><copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"><license>https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/</license></copyright><link href="https://open.pilgrimag.es/camino-portugues"><text>Camino Portugués (Central)</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Camino Portugués (Central)</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="41.143086" lon="-8.611049"/><trkpt lat="41.143105" lon="-8.610945"/><trkpt lat="41.143192" lon="-8.610501"/><trkpt lat="41.143201" lon="-8.610448"/><trkpt lat="41.143211" lon="-8.610396"/><trkpt lat="41.143273" lon="-8.610319"/><trkpt lat="41.143076" lon="-8.611109"/><trkpt lat="41.143086" lon="-8.611049"/><trkpt lat="41.143052" lon="-8.611237"/><trkpt lat="41.143076" lon="-8.611109"/><trkpt lat="41.142956" lon="-8.611532"/><trkpt lat="41.143037" lon="-8.611352"/><trkpt lat="41.143052" lon="-8.611237"/><trkpt lat="41.142941" lon="-8.611559"/><trkpt lat="41.142956" lon="-8.611532"/><trkpt lat="41.142738" lon="-8.611876"/><trkpt lat="41.142743" lon="-8.611847"/><trkpt lat="41.142759" lon="-8.611756"/><trkpt lat="41.142907" lon="-8.611764"/><trkpt lat="41.142920" lon="-8.611643"/><trkpt lat="41.142941" lon="-8.611559"/><trkpt lat="41.142646" lon="-8.612322"/><trkpt lat="41.142656" lon="-8.612275"/><trkpt lat="41.142693" lon="-8.612089"/><trkpt lat="41.142738" lon="-8.611876"/><trkpt lat="41.142509" lon="-8.612263"/><trkpt lat="41.142611" lon="-8.612308"/><trkpt lat="41.142628" lon="-8.612315"/><trkpt lat="41.142646" lon="-8.61232